{"id":1375,"date":"2020-11-27T15:24:10","date_gmt":"2020-11-27T23:24:10","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1375"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:31","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:31","slug":"rokit-counters","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/rokit-counters\/","title":{"rendered":"Counters"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215f3a6d89\" name=\"6a2215f3a6d89\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>How to Make Counters<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]We can use counters to break our code into steps inside of\u00a0<em>void loop<\/em>. This way we can have our code broken up in to simple steps. To do this we will have a\u00a0<em>variable\u00a0<\/em>to keep track of our current step. Then we will use a series of<em>\u00a0if statements\u00a0<\/em>to have each of our steps. Then at the end of each step we will have it change the counter to move on to the next step.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int counter = 0;\r\n \r\nvoid setup()\r\n{\r\n \r\n}\r\n \r\nvoid loop()\r\n{\r\n  if (counter == 0)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/ code for step 1\r\n    counter = 1;\r\n  }\r\n  else if (counter == 1)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/ code for step 2\r\n    counter = 2;\r\n  }\r\n  else if (counter == 2)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/ code for step 3\r\n    counter = 3;\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215f3a6e91\" name=\"6a2215f3a6e91\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add an if statement into an if statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Each time through the<em>\u00a0loop<\/em>\u00a0this code will do the next step in the process. If you would like it to not always move on to the next step you can have the changing of the counter value inside of another\u00a0<em>if statement<\/em>\u00a0so that it will not change to the next step until the condition is met.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int counter = 0;\r\n \r\nvoid setup()\r\n{\r\n \r\n}\r\n \r\nvoid loop()\r\n{\r\n  if (counter == 0)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/ code for step 1\r\n \r\n    if (condition1)\r\n    {\r\n      counter = 1;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  else if (counter == 1)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/ code for step 2\r\n \r\n    if (condition2)\r\n    {\r\n      counter = 2;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  else if (counter == 2)\r\n  {\r\n    \/\/ code for step 3\r\n \r\n    if (condition3)\r\n    {\r\n      counter = 3;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215f3a6ef8\" name=\"6a2215f3a6ef8\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Here is an example code for using counters to move through a three step program.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">int counter = 0;\r\n \r\nvoid setup()\r\n{\r\n  Serial.begin(9600);\r\n}\r\n \r\nvoid loop()\r\n{\r\n  if (counter == 0)\r\n  {\r\n    Serial.println(\"first step\");\r\n    counter = 1;\r\n  }\r\n  else if (counter == 1)\r\n  {\r\n    Serial.println(\"second step\");\r\n    counter = 2;\r\n  }\r\n  else if (counter == 2)\r\n  {\r\n    Serial.println(\"third step\");\r\n    counter = 3;\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>This will have it print out this:<\/p>\n<p>first step<\/p>\n<p>second step<\/p>\n<p>third step<\/p>\n<p>Then it will not keep repeating, since there is no step for when counter is equal to 3.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215f3a6f42\" name=\"6a2215f3a6f42\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This video teaches this concept as well.[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=oeyO4ZLY9Ug&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 5 How to Make Counters [vc_column_text]We can use counters to break our code into steps inside of\u00a0void loop. This way we can have our code broken up in&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/rokit-counters\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1732,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1760,1777,1815,1808,1793,626,1533,1438,144,63,209],"lesson-tag":[2163,2123,2182,2118,2122,2171,2117],"class_list":["post-1375","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-if-statements","lesson-tag-loops","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-variables","module-programming","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1375","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1375\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1376,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1375\/revisions\/1376"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.lea